        "id": 1348429
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-01-11T22:20:17Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It all boils down to the order in which the modules are loaded (this, the order, is supposed to be configurable - if I got things right). This will require a dedicated module that will register for the hook and upon it being triggered, make decision whether the workaround is to be enabled or not. As long as that module is loaded first (and that is to be controlled by vendors) the hook\u0027s callback will get called upon each driver being loaded afterwords, thus giving a way to decide whether to apply the workaround or not. \nI\u0027m not sure whether having it being considered on a per-bus basis would make much of a difference , unless I am missing smth, which is very much possible (?)",
      "parentUuid": "b0c9e04f_92d88e2c",
